 "concept": "Red-brick Victorian factory complex in the steampunk kit. Silhouette: one landmark clock tower (octagon, tall, spire roof) rising well over 1.8x the next volume, flanked by a wide sawtooth-roofed machine hall and a lower boiler house with twin smoke stacks. A low living/office wing and a workshop ground the composition. Materials: red brick walls (60), stone brick piers and polished deepslate base (30), copper trim and glowing lamp bands (10), with a dark slate roof and a copper-green spire. Interiors are big: machine hall 11 high and 21x27, boiler house 10 high, workshop 7 high. Detail goes outward: chimneys on the boiler house, gears on the clock tower face and hall, pipe runs on the process hall, a bridge across the yard to the workshop, and a terraced platform base.",
